<<<< This is a placeholder for the compiled Zygisk library >>>>

To build the actual library:

1. Compile main.cpp using Android NDK:
   cd src
   mkdir build && cd build
   cmake .. \
     -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=$NDK/build/cmake/android.toolchain.cmake \
     -DANDROID_ABI=arm64-v8a \
     -DANDROID_PLATFORM=android-26 \
     -DANDROID_STL=c++_static
   make -j$(nproc)

2. Copy the compiled library:
   cp libpubg_suite.so ../../zygisk/arm64-v8a.so

3. Re-zip the module:
   cd ..
   zip -r ../pubg_full_suite.zip . -x "src/build/*"

After building, replace this placeholder with the actual compiled .so file.
